I think I tried that with one healer and didn't make it very far.
Inevitably, something gets close to you, and it just doesn't take very
many attacks to kill you when you're naked and XL1.  Not that non-naked
healers start with great armor either, but at least they can pick up
decent stuff on way.

I found the best things to compensate for being naked in the early game
were (1) a good weapon or attack spell to keep things from getting too
many attacks on you, (2) to gain HP quickly so you can withstand a few
rounds of combat when needed, and (3) use your assets - don't save that
?oTel, /oCold, or prayer for later.

